WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.440
A motor neuron is built by combinations of transcription factors acting in stages.

2
00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:11.160
The code first makes a motor neuron.

3
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.860
Then it helps decide which muscle its axon will reach.

4
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.920
That is why making a motor neuron is only part of the story.

5
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:23.900
Follow the code from a stripe in the neural tube to a neuron connected to muscle.

6
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.450
Sonic hedgehog sets up a gradient across the neural tube.

7
00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:31.470
Progenitors read their position in it.

8
00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:34.470
One stripe, pMN, makes motor neurons.

9
00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.250
Its dividing cells carry Olig2.

10
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.030
Around the final division, the cell turns on a new set.

11
00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:49.423
Isl1 or its relative Isl2, Lhx3, and Mnx1 mark the newly differentiated motor

12
00:00:49.423 --> 00:00:52.703
neuron. But a marker is not a unique label.

13
00:00:53.623 --> 00:00:57.343
Lhx3 also appears in neighbouring V2 interneurons.

14
00:00:58.163 --> 00:00:59.643
Its partners change its output.

15
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:07.177
In chick, Lhx3 without Isl1 binds NLI and promotes V2 interneuron genes.

16
00:01:08.077 --> 00:01:11.757
Add Isl1, and a different complex promotes motor-neuron genes.

17
00:01:12.597 --> 00:01:13.697
The combination matters.

18
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:18.570
Delete Isl1 in mouse, and motor neurons are not generated.

19
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:25.370
Delete Mnx1, and they form but transiently show V2 features, with disordered columns

20
00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:30.350
and axons. Making a cell and maintaining its identity are different jobs.

21
00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:32.823
Now, which motor neuron?

22
00:01:33.803 --> 00:01:36.183
Hox proteins record position along the cord.

23
00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:39.563
With FoxP1, they assign columns and pools.

24
00:01:40.423 --> 00:01:43.003
The lateral motor column supplies limb muscles.

25
00:01:43.923 --> 00:01:45.323
A pool supplies one muscle.

26
00:01:46.423 --> 00:01:49.303
Delete Foxp1 in mouse, and motor neurons still form.

27
00:01:50.083 --> 00:01:52.663
But limb and autonomic column identities fail.

28
00:01:53.523 --> 00:01:57.023
In the limb, axons appear to choose paths and muscles at random.

29
00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:00.073
The code also reaches the axon.

30
00:02:01.073 --> 00:02:06.973
Lateral cells of the limb column express Lhx1, which ensures a dorsal trajectory in

31
00:02:06.973 --> 00:02:10.353
the limb. Without it, their axons lose that preference.

32
00:02:11.313 --> 00:02:14.393
Eph receptors and ephrins are part of the guidance machinery.

33
00:02:15.433 --> 00:02:16.653
Identity helps set the route.

34
00:02:17.617 --> 00:02:20.037
Use that developmental logic in a dish.

35
00:02:20.937 --> 00:02:25.197
In mouse embryonic stem cells, retinoic acid promotes spinal character.

36
00:02:25.997 --> 00:02:28.617
A Hedgehog agonist pushes cells toward pMN.

37
00:02:29.717 --> 00:02:30.717
Motor neurons follow.

38
00:02:31.337 --> 00:02:35.017
This basic protocol gives mostly medial motor column cells.

39
00:02:35.817 --> 00:02:37.777
Making one named pool remains harder.

40
00:02:38.557 --> 00:02:42.517
The code can build motor neurons, but its fine detail is still incomplete.
